      >
      IMGRESOURCEFLAGS 11
    >
    <ITEM
      POSITION 1051.5
      SNAPOFFS 0
      LENGTH 11
      LOOP 1
      ALLTAKES 0
      FADEIN 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
      FADEOUT 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
      MUTE 0 0
      SEL 0
      IGUID {0DEFEE1D-50DC-4E50-A36D-1EAE16F88DE2}
      IID 36401
      <NOTES
        |Why here in Denmark: I have been sexton here man and boy thirty years.
      >
      IMGRESOURCEFLAGS 11
    >
    <ITEM
      POSITION 1066.5
      SNAPOFFS 0
      LENGTH 11
      LOOP 1
      ALLTAKES 0
      FADEIN 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
      FADEOUT 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
      MUTE 0 0
      SEL 0
      IGUID {0A66A20C-04BA-47A5-925E-5C74795A7E5E}
      IID 36404
      <NOTES
        |How long will a man lie i' the earth ere he rot?
      >
      IMGRESOURCEFLAGS 11
    >
    <ITEM
      POSITION 1081.5
      SNAPOFFS 0
      LENGTH 11
      LOOP 1
      ALLTAKES 0
      FADEIN 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
      FADEOUT 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
      MUTE 0 0
      SEL 0
      IGUID {3F300E62-831E-4D31-A57E-FB0AF28468C9}
      IID 36407
      <NOTES
        |Faith if he be not rotten before he die--and we have many pocky corses now-a-days that will scarce hold the laying in--
      >
      IMGRESOURCEFLAGS 11
    >
    <ITEM
      POSITION 1096.5
      SNAPOFFS 0
      LENGTH 11
      LOOP 1
      ALLTAKES 0
      FADEIN 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
      FADEOUT 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
      MUTE 0 0
      SEL 0
      IGUID {4C9D9D91-5727-437E-ACF2-B9AD51B0E067}
      IID 36410
      <NOTES
        |He must build churches then.
      >
      IMGRESOURCEFLAGS 11
    >
    <ITEM
      POSITION 1111.5
      SNAPOFFS 0
      LENGTH 11
      LOOP 1
      ALLTAKES 0
      FADEIN 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
      FADEOUT 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
      MUTE 0 0
      SEL 0
      IGUID {01D5534B-F4D6-4665-AFAC-2005425ED55B}
      IID 36413
      <NOTES
        |No I tell thee he will keep no mean in the talking to himself: words words words.
      >
      IMGRESOURCEFLAGS 11
    >
    <ITEM
      POSITION 1126.5
      SNAPOFFS 0
      LENGTH 11
      LOOP 1
      ALLTAKES 0
      FADEIN 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
      FADEOUT 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
      MUTE 0 0
      SEL 0
      IGUID {3DD58749-34AA-451F-B623-AEDE815DF9CF}
      IID 36416
      <NOTES
        |Alas poor Yorick! I knew him Horatio: a fellow of infinite jest of most excellent fancy.
      >
      IMGRESOURCEFLAGS 11
    >
    <ITEM
      POSITION 1141.5
      SNAPOFFS 0
      LENGTH 11
      LOOP 1
      ALLTAKES 0
      FADEIN 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
      FADEOUT 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
      MUTE 0 0
      SEL 0
      IGUID {17B497A9-BD60-4AB2-969F-0CBF930610D2}
      IID 36419
      <NOTES
        |He hath borne me on his back a thousand times; and now how abhorred in my imagination it is!
      >
      IMGRESOURCEFLAGS 11
    >
    <ITEM
      POSITION 1156.5
      SNAPOFFS 0
      LENGTH 11
      LOOP 1
      ALLTAKES 0
      FADEIN 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
      FADEOUT 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
      MUTE 0 0
      SEL 0
      IGUID {8E049738-436B-4000-8592-67D0BAA8F944}
      IID 36422
      <NOTES
        |My gorge rises at it. Here hung those lips that I have kissed I know not how oft.
      >
      IMGRESOURCEFLAGS 11
    >
    <ITEM
      POSITION 1171.5
      SNAPOFFS 0
      LENGTH 11
      LOOP 1
      ALLTAKES 0
      FADEIN 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
      FADEOUT 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
      MUTE 0 0
      SEL 0
      IGUID {589F2892-FD73-489B-8F38-34A178C4F2B1}
      IID 36425
      <NOTES
        |Where be your gibes now? your gambols? your songs? your flashes of merriment that were wont to set the table on a roar?
      >
      IMGRESOURCEFLAGS 11
    >
    <ITEM
      POSITION 1186.5
      SNAPOFFS 0
      LENGTH 11
      LOOP 1
      ALLTAKES 0
      FADEIN 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
      FADEOUT 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
      MUTE 0 0
      SEL 0
      IGUID {941D9D6E-2221-4B59-BCF8-7307E69CDB30}
      IID 36428
      <NOTES
        |Not one now to mock your own grinning? quite chap-fallen? Now get you to my lady's chamber and tell her let her paint an inch thick to this favour she must come; make her laugh at that.
      >
      IMGRESOURCEFLAGS 11
    >
    <ITEM
      POSITION 1201.5
      SNAPOFFS 0
      LENGTH 11
      LOOP 1
      ALLTAKES 0
      FADEIN 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
      FADEOUT 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
      MUTE 0 0
      SEL 0
      IGUID {DC210673-1A31-4C6A-95A4-94216B976EE4}
      IID 36431
      <NOTES
        |Prithee Horatio tell me one thing.
      >
      IMGRESOURCEFLAGS 11
    >
    <ITEM
      POSITION 1216.5
      SNAPOFFS 0
      LENGTH 11
      LOOP 1
      ALLTAKES 0
      FADEIN 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
      FADEOUT 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
      MUTE 0 0
      SEL 0
      IGUID {AF0C7940-99A4-4603-9003-FA95B6B06A1E}
      IID 36434
      <NOTES
        |What's that my lord?
      >
      IMGRESOURCEFLAGS 11
    >
    <ITEM
      POSITION 1231.5
      SNAPOFFS 0
      LENGTH 11
      LOOP 1
      ALLTAKES 0
      FADEIN 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
      FADEOUT 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
      MUTE 0 0
      SEL 0
      IGUID {47BF89C2-BCF4-4C40-BFD8-5FC5E071BAA7}
      IID 36437
      <NOTES
        |Dost thou think Alexander looked o' this fashion i' the earth?
      >
      IMGRESOURCEFLAGS 11
    >
    <ITEM
      POSITION 1246.5
      SNAPOFFS 0
      LENGTH 11
      LOOP 1
      ALLTAKES 0
      FADEIN 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
      FADEOUT 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
      MUTE 0 0
      SEL 0
      IGUID {1D607378-F69A-4E24-A124-901EDF7DD337}
      IID 36440
      <NOTES
        |E'en so.
      >
      IMGRESOURCEFLAGS 11
    >
    <ITEM
      POSITION 1261.5
      SNAPOFFS 0
      LENGTH 11
      LOOP 1
      ALLTAKES 0
      FADEIN 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
      FADEOUT 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
      MUTE 0 0
      SEL 0
      IGUID {CE475385-9C29-479E-AC59-D1103FF6A2CF}
      IID 36443
      <NOTES
        |To what base uses we may return Horatio! Why may not imagination trace the noble dust of Alexander till he find it stopping a bunghole?
      >
      IMGRESOURCEFLAGS 11
    >
    <ITEM
      POSITION 1276.5
      SNAPOFFS 0
      LENGTH 11
      LOOP 1
      ALLTAKES 0
      FADEIN 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
      FADEOUT 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
      MUTE 0 0
      SEL 0
      IGUID {A9743C63-16DE-4D73-BF51-B37808236B35}
      IID 36446
      <NOTES
        |'Twere to consider too curiously to consider so.
      >
      IMGRESOURCEFLAGS 11
    >
    <ITEM
      POSITION 1291.5
      SNAPOFFS 0
      LENGTH 11
      LOOP 1
      ALLTAKES 0
      FADEIN 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
      FADEOUT 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
      MUTE 0 0
      SEL 0
      IGUID {59231610-D1CF-4620-B2FF-79E5A94D3F74}
      IID 36449
      <NOTES
        |No faith not a jot; but to follow him thither with modesty enough and likelihood to lead it: as thus: Alexander died Alexander was buried Alexander returneth into dust; the dust is earth; of earth we make loam; and why of that loam whereto he was converted might they not stop a beer-barrel?
      >
      IMGRESOURCEFLAGS 11
    >
    <ITEM
      POSITION 1306.5
      SNAPOFFS 0
      LENGTH 11
      LOOP 1
      ALLTAKES 0
      FADEIN 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
      FADEOUT 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
      MUTE 0 0
      SEL 0
      IGUID {5B4B423B-C7CB-4000-814D-12D5C85AB78D}
      IID 36452
      <NOTES
        |Imperious Caesar dead and turned to clay might stop a hole to keep the wind away.
      >
      IMGRESOURCEFLAGS 11
    >
    <ITEM
      POSITION 1321.5
      SNAPOFFS 0
      LENGTH 11
      LOOP 1
      ALLTAKES 0
      FADEIN 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
      FADEOUT 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
      MUTE 0 0
      SEL 0
      IGUID {5F7C0823-41AF-4D6B-9A94-22689D8492AE}
      IID 36455
      <NOTES
        |O that that earth which kept the world in awe should patch a wall t' expel the winter's flaw!
      >
      IMGRESOURCEFLAGS 11
    >
